    {
      "filename": "Bulevardul Unirii and the Palace of the Parliament - Communist Romania's answer to Paris's Avenue des Champs-Élysées (11321610195).jpg",
      "title": "File:Bulevardul Unirii and the Palace of the Parliament - Communist Romania's answer to Paris's Avenue des Champs-Élysées (11321610195).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bf/Bulevardul_Unirii_and_the_Palace_of_the_Parliament_-_Communist_Romania%27s_answer_to_Paris%27s_Avenue_des_Champs-%C3%89lys%C3%A9es_%2811321610195%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bulevardul_Unirii_and_the_Palace_of_the_Parliament_-_Communist_Romania%27s_answer_to_Paris%27s_Avenue_des_Champs-%C3%89lys%C3%A9es_(11321610195).jpg",
      "width": 4288,
      "height": 2848,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Jorge Láscar from Australia",
      "description": "Bulevardul Unirii (Unification Boulevard) is a major thoroughfare in central Bucharest, Romania. It connects Alba Iulia Square with Constitution Square, and also runs through Unification Square. The Constitution Square end features the Palace of the Parliament.\n\nFollowing the 1977 Vrancea earthquake, Bucharest's city center suffered significant damage, and a large number of historic buildings were demolished to make way for the new Centrul Civic (Civic Center; see systematization and Ceaușima). As part of the project, Bulevardul Unirii was to be Communist Romania's answer to Paris's Avenue des Champs-Élysées, with a length of 3,500 m. Construction began on June 25, 1984. Initially called Bulevardul Victoria Socialismului (Victory of Socialism Boulevard), the road is lined with socialist-realism inspired buildings [Wikipedia.org]",
      "dateCreated": "Taken on 24 August 2012, 20:21",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "palace-of-the-parliament-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "sxfs",
      "mediumPath": "_m/s/x/f/s/palace-of-the-parliament-wp/bulevardul-unirii-and-the-pala-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/s/x/f/s/palace-of-the-parliament-wp/bulevardul-unirii-and-the-pala-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Bulevardul Unirii and the Palace of the Parliament - Communist Romania's answer to Paris's Avenue des Champs-Élysées (11320789445).jpg",
      "title": "File:Bulevardul Unirii and the Palace of the Parliament - Communist Romania's answer to Paris's Avenue des Champs-Élysées (11320789445).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/Bulevardul_Unirii_and_the_Palace_of_the_Parliament_-_Communist_Romania%27s_answer_to_Paris%27s_Avenue_des_Champs-%C3%89lys%C3%A9es_%2811320789445%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bulevardul_Unirii_and_the_Palace_of_the_Parliament_-_Communist_Romania%27s_answer_to_Paris%27s_Avenue_des_Champs-%C3%89lys%C3%A9es_(11320789445).jpg",
      "width": 4288,
      "height": 2848,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Jorge Láscar from Australia",
      "description": "Bulevardul Unirii (Unification Boulevard) is a major thoroughfare in central Bucharest, Romania. It connects Alba Iulia Square with Constitution Square, and also runs through Unification Square. The Constitution Square end features the Palace of the Parliament.\n\nFollowing the 1977 Vrancea earthquake, Bucharest's city center suffered significant damage, and a large number of historic buildings were demolished to make way for the new Centrul Civic (Civic Center; see systematization and Ceaușima). As part of the project, Bulevardul Unirii was to be Communist Romania's answer to Paris's Avenue des Champs-Élysées, with a length of 3,500 m. Construction began on June 25, 1984. Initially called Bulevardul Victoria Socialismului (Victory of Socialism Boulevard), the road is lined with socialist-realism inspired buildings [Wikipedia.org]",
      "dateCreated": "Taken on 24 August 2012, 20:13",
